Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, in the past, mas malaki po ang funding niyan.

5124
06:36:37,280 --> 06:36:38,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron po tayong, ayan, no?

5125
06:36:39,240 --> 06:36:41,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Starting from Bayanihan 2, yung panahon ng pandemic.

5126
06:36:42,660 --> 06:36:44,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dun po, malaki yung unang naglaan.

5127
06:36:45,340 --> 06:36:46,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 3 billion pesos.

5128
06:36:47,280 --> 06:36:49,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 1.316 billion pesos.

5129
06:36:49,300 --> 06:36:51,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This is data provided by the DOTR.

5130
06:36:52,340 --> 06:36:52,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

5131
06:36:53,160 --> 06:36:54,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And then, from 2022,

5132
06:36:55,520 --> 06:36:58,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: balik tayo dun sa graph, dun sa table, yung iyan.

5133
06:36:59,600 --> 06:37:01,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para mas visual po, makita natin.

5134
06:37:03,840 --> 06:37:05,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2022 po, 2 billion.

5135
06:37:06,080 --> 06:37:07,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2 billion ang appropriations.

5136
06:37:08,440 --> 06:37:08,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

5137
06:37:08,720 --> 06:37:11,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And then, 2023, 705 million.

5138
06:37:11,860 --> 06:37:13,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Then, umakyat muli to 1 billion.

5139
06:37:14,220 --> 06:37:15,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Noong 2020,

5140
06:37:15,180 --> 06:37:15,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2024.

5141
06:37:16,080 --> 06:37:17,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero from 2025 onward,

5142
06:37:18,800 --> 06:37:21,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: paliit na, dramatically, lumiit na po.

5143
06:37:21,940 --> 06:37:25,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, 2025, 60 million.

5144
06:37:26,740 --> 06:37:29,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos, 2026, 69 million.

5145
06:37:30,520 --> 06:37:33,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos, ngayon, ang proposed na lang, as I said earlier,

5146
06:37:33,820 --> 06:37:35,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: is 33 million.

5147
06:37:36,440 --> 06:37:40,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, mula sa 2 billion, ngayon, 33 million na lang po.

5148
06:37:42,500 --> 06:37:43,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang paliwanag?

5149
06:37:44,300 --> 06:37:45,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit ganyan na lang po?

5150
06:37:45,160 --> 06:37:46,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang proposal natin?

5151
06:37:47,400 --> 06:37:51,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lalo na in the past few years and for 2027?

5152
06:37:52,260 --> 06:37:59,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano naman po ang mga siklista, pedestrian, at PWDs?

5153
06:37:59,500 --> 06:38:05,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na hindi lang po mga motorista ang kailangang

5154
06:38:05,580 --> 06:38:12,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: servisyon ng gobyerno, diba?

5155
06:38:12,200 --> 06:38:14,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa kanilang karapatang maglakbay.

5156
06:38:15,160 --> 06:38:20,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, bakit po napakaliit na ng proposed budget for active transport?

5157
06:38:20,740 --> 06:38:26,060
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Mr. Speaker, dear colleague, yan po ang isang, the sad part of it.

5158
06:38:26,340 --> 06:38:31,600
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Ang request po ng DOTR is 1.2 billion for the active transport.

5159
06:38:33,280 --> 06:38:39,560
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Unfortunately, 33 million lang po ang nailaan or equivalent of 5 kilometers.

5160
06:38:39,560 --> 06:38:45,040
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Which, nagpapatulong po ang DOTR sa Kongreso na madagdagan po ito.

5161
06:38:45,160 --> 06:38:46,620
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: May ibalik po yung request.

5162
06:38:47,060 --> 06:38:56,500
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Dahil po nabawasan during the budget legislation at yan na po ang naging desisyon ng Department of Budget and Management.

5163
06:38:56,840 --> 06:39:00,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, nabanggit siyo po yung 33 million is good for?

5164
06:39:00,640 --> 06:39:01,220
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: 5 kilometers.

5165
06:39:01,400 --> 06:39:02,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 5 kilometers.

5166
06:39:02,680 --> 06:39:02,980
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Dear colleague.

5167
06:39:02,980 --> 06:39:08,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 5 kilometers of pathways, cycle or pedestrian.

5168
06:39:09,220 --> 06:39:09,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

5169
06:39:10,240 --> 06:39:12,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, yan din po ang isang tanong natin.

5170
06:39:12,440 --> 06:39:13,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course.

5171
06:39:14,040 --> 06:39:14,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah.

5172
06:39:14,300 --> 06:39:18,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang sponsor po natin ngayon, naka-wheelchair pa po.

5173
06:39:18,960 --> 06:39:21,020
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Ako po ang una makikinabang sa Safe Path Race, dear colleague.

5174
06:39:21,020 --> 06:39:21,600
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Tama po yan.

5175
06:39:22,020 --> 06:39:27,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam nyo, ako rin po, siklista, matagal na.

5176
06:39:28,060 --> 06:39:32,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At dahil sa kakapusan ng cycling infrastructure, ilang beses na rin na aksidente.

5177
06:39:33,160 --> 06:39:35,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: One time, nabalian po ako ng ankle.

5178
06:39:36,480 --> 06:39:39,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kailangan ko magsaklay.

5179
06:39:39,660 --> 06:39:43,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At naranasan ko yung paglalakad sa mga pedestrian lane natin.

5180
06:39:44,300 --> 06:39:49,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na talagang challenge para sa mga persons with disabilities, no?

5181
06:39:50,020 --> 06:39:58,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung hindi pantay na sidewalk, basag-basag yung simento, papalit-palit yung level.

5182
06:39:59,280 --> 06:40:01,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In many cases, walang sidewalk.

5183
06:40:02,600 --> 06:40:03,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganun po, no?

5184
06:40:04,020 --> 06:40:09,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya po, sinusuportahan natin ito definitely.

5185
06:40:09,720 --> 06:40:12,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero at the same time, kailangan natin ng transparency.

5186
06:40:13,420 --> 06:40:13,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So,

5187
06:40:14,300 --> 06:40:16,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa mga submission nyo po, walang nakalagay.

5188
06:40:16,760 --> 06:40:22,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magkano po ba ang costing nyo per kilometer of cycle pathway?

5189
06:40:22,700 --> 06:40:28,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi po, kinumpute natin yung Bayanihan budget.

5190
06:40:28,920 --> 06:40:34,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bayanihan to budget, that was 1.09 billion.

5191
06:40:35,340 --> 06:40:38,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For a total, ayon sa inyong accomplishment report,

5192
06:40:38,260 --> 06:40:43,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for a total of 498 kilometers of cycle paths,

5193
06:40:44,300 --> 06:40:47,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kung i-de-divide po natin, lumalabas,

5194
06:40:48,000 --> 06:40:50,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: una-muna, magkano po yung costing nyo?

5195
06:40:51,100 --> 06:40:54,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tignan natin kung magkakorespond sa kinumpute ko.

5196
06:40:57,940 --> 06:41:02,780
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Mr. Speaker, dear colleague, there are three classifications of the pathway, no?

5197
06:41:03,400 --> 06:41:05,680
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: May class 1, class 2, and class 3.

5198
06:41:06,820 --> 06:41:10,640
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Ang class 1 po, pag new pathway construction,

5199
06:41:10,640 --> 06:41:12,820
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: the estimated cost is around 10 million.

5200
06:41:12,820 --> 06:41:14,820
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Per kilometer.

5201
06:41:14,820 --> 06:41:15,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Per kilometer. Okay.

5202
06:41:16,620 --> 06:41:22,220
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Then, sa class 2, may, ano, may, with physical separators,

5203
06:41:22,220 --> 06:41:26,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: the cost will be more or less 5.4 million.

5204
06:41:26,320 --> 06:41:26,820
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Alright.

5205
06:41:26,820 --> 06:41:27,820
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Per kilometer.

5206
06:41:27,820 --> 06:41:28,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Okay.

5207
06:41:28,320 --> 06:41:32,820
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Then, for class 3, ayan yung tinatawag na pavement marking only.

5208
06:41:32,820 --> 06:41:34,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Yung pintura lang po?

5209
06:41:34,320 --> 06:41:34,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes.

5210
06:41:34,820 --> 06:41:36,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Magkano po yan?

5211
06:41:36,320 --> 06:41:38,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Mga reflectorized po yan.

5212
06:41:38,320 --> 06:41:41,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: 2.5 million per kilometer.

5213
06:41:41,320 --> 06:41:42,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2.5 million per kilometer.

5214
06:41:42,320 --> 06:41:52,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, sa computation ko po, yung 498 kilometers reported for the Bayanihan II funding of 1.09 billion,

5215
06:41:52,320 --> 06:41:57,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pumapatak sa 2.1 million per kilometer.

5216
06:41:57,320 --> 06:42:02,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So mukhang pintura lang po talaga to. Parang ganun. Tama po ba?

5217
06:42:02,320 --> 06:42:03,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Combination po yan.

5218
06:42:03,320 --> 06:42:10,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Combination. Pero, well, it would seem that most of it ay yung type 3 na tinatawag ninyo.

5219
06:42:10,320 --> 06:42:11,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

5220
06:42:11,320 --> 06:42:21,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, again, magkano po ang proposal? Napaka, mahirap naman po tanggapin na 5 kilometers lang.

5221
06:42:21,320 --> 06:42:24,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: 1.2 billion, dear colleague.

5222
06:42:24,320 --> 06:42:25,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magkano po?

5223
06:42:25,320 --> 06:42:26,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: 1.2 billion.

5224
06:42:26,320 --> 06:42:27,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: 1.2 billion.

5225
06:42:27,320 --> 06:42:28,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pesos.

5226
06:42:28,320 --> 06:42:34,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And how much, ano po ang kung breakdown nitong 1.2 billion na ito?

5227
06:42:34,320 --> 06:42:51,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: For 1.2 billion, it's more or less 180 kilometers of new and maintained bike lanes and walkways.

5228
06:42:51,320 --> 06:42:52,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Anong type po?

5229
06:42:52,320 --> 06:42:56,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What type of pathways?

5230
06:42:56,320 --> 06:43:01,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Combination na po ito ng class 1, class 2, and class 3.

5231
06:43:01,320 --> 06:43:02,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: So all three types. Ganun po. No?

5232
06:43:02,320 --> 06:43:13,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Noted po. Pero malinaw po ang mandato dito sa special provision.

5233
06:43:13,320 --> 06:43:22,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bike lanes should have smooth pavement, be free of hazards, and with durable physical separation from mixed traffic lanes.

5234
06:43:22,320 --> 06:43:31,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung sa class 1, class 2, class 3 na sinasabit nyo, kung pintura lang, does that count as durable physical separation?

5235
06:43:31,320 --> 06:43:34,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po, dear colleague.

5236
06:43:34,320 --> 06:43:41,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So malinaw po ang mandato dito. Type 1. Ano ba yung term? Class or type?

5237
06:43:41,320 --> 06:43:42,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Class 1.

5238
06:43:42,320 --> 06:43:43,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Class 1.

5239
06:43:43,320 --> 06:43:44,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Class 1.

5240
06:43:44,320 --> 06:43:45,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: New pathway.

5241
06:43:45,320 --> 06:43:51,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung pathway. Yung class 2, ano nga po yung class 2? May barrier.

5242
06:43:51,320 --> 06:43:59,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Yung class 2, may carriageway siya pero may separator.

5243
06:43:59,320 --> 06:44:00,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May physical separator.

5244
06:44:00,320 --> 06:44:01,320
Rep. Edwin Ongchuan: Yes.

5245
06:44:01,320 --> 06:44:04,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Parang yung mga concrete or

5246
